.TH SINDOOK-ROTATE 1 "2026-08-31" "sindook 0.11.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook-rotate \- retire an old identity across many sealed files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook rotate -i
\fIIDENTITY\fP (\fB\-to\fP \fIRECIPIENT\fP)... [\fB\-deep\fP]
[\fB\-jobs\fP \fIN\fP] [\fB\-glob\fP \fIPATTERN\fP]... [\fB\-json\fP]
\fIDIR\fP|\fIFILE\fP...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Retires an identity from sealed files in bulk. Every candidate file is
opened with \fIIDENTITY\fP; files it opens are rewrapped to the \fB\-to\fP
recipients, files it cannot open are reported as skipped. Use it when
one identity must lose access to everything: offboarding, a
compromised key, or a periodic hygiene pass. The identity being
retired must be held, because authenticated opening is what decides
which files match; the current format has no metadata filter.
.PP
Rotation replaces each file's slot set with exactly the \fB\-to\fP
recipients. Fast mode keeps the payload ciphertext; \fB\-deep\fP
re-encrypts under a fresh file key. Fast mode does not revoke
recipients who already hold a copy of the old file. Files are staged
beside their original path and replaced only after a successful
write.
.PP
Directory operands are walked for *.sindook files; explicit
\fIFILE\fP operands are attempted whatever their name. Every file is
attempted even if an earlier one fails, and the exit code is non-zero
only when a rewrap failed; skipped files are not failures.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fP \fIIDENTITY\fP
the identity being retired (required)
.TP
\fB\-identity-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP
read a protected identity's passphrase from \fIFILE\fP
.TP
\fB\-to\fP \fIRECIPIENT\fP
new recipient, repeatable; the replacement file is sealed to exactly
these recipients
.TP
\fB\-deep\fP
re-encrypt the payload under a fresh file key
.TP
\fB\-jobs\fP \fIN\fP
rotate up to N files concurrently (default: up to 4 for multiple
files, 1 for a single file)
.TP
\fB\-glob\fP \fIPATTERN\fP
add files matched by a portable filesystem pattern, repeatable
.TP
\fB\-json\fP
print one machine-readable JSON array with per-file status instead of
human-readable lines
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sindook rotate -i old.key -to @team backups/
sindook rotate -i offboarded.key -to personal.key.pub -deep -jobs 8 vault/
sindook rotate -i old.key -to alice.pub -glob "archive/*.sindook"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sindook (1),
.BR sindook-rewrap (1),
.BR sindook-verify (1)
